{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YZFPTz75RERn3Bwg1Zh8xx","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t[\n2\t  {\n3\t    \"name\": \"core_revalidation_clean\",\n4\t    \"description\": \"Re-run Phase B on clean data with 3 seeds. Treatment vs baseline on IID crescendo + topic-anchored benign.\\n\",\n5\t    \"results\": {\n6\t      \"treatment_k1_f1\": 1.0,\n7\t      \"treatment_k2_f1\": 1.0,\n8\t      \"treatment_full_f1\": 1.0,\n9\t      \"baseline_k1_f1\": 0.968,\n10\t      \"baseline_k2_f1\": 0.978,\n11\t      \"baseline_full_f1\": 1.0,\n12\t      \"tfidf_all_k_f1\": 1.0,\n13\t      \"max_delta_pp\": 3.2,\n14\t      \"pass_criteria_5pp\": false,\n15\t      \"seed_std_treatment\": 0.0,\n16\t      \"seed_std_baseline_k1\": 0.033\n17\t    },\n18\t    \"tables\": [\n19\t      {\n20\t        \"caption\": \"Table 1: IID Detection Performance (3-seed mean ± std)\",\n21\t        \"rows\": [\n22\t          {\n23\t            \"model\": \"Treatment (ours)\",\n24\t            \"k1\": \"1.000±0.000\",\n25\t            \"k2\": \"1.000±0.000\",\n26\t            \"k3\": \"1.000±0.000\",\n27\t            \"full\": \"1.000±0.000\"\n28\t          },\n29\t          {\n30\t            \"model\": \"Baseline (vanilla)\",\n31\t            \"k1\": \"0.968±0.033\",\n32\t            \"k2\": \"0.978±0.016\",\n33\t            \"k3\": \"0.987±0.000\",\n34\t            \"full\": \"1.000±0.000\"\n35\t          },\n36\t          {\n37\t            \"model\": \"TF-IDF + LR\",\n38\t            \"k1\": \"1.000\",\n39\t            \"k2\": \"1.000\",\n40\t            \"k3\": \"1.000\",\n41\t            \"full\": \"1.000\"\n42\t          }\n43\t        ]\n44\t      }\n45\t    ],\n46\t    \"figures\": [],\n47\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 2 的致命评论：\\\"Table 1 shows that the baseline already achieves F1≥0.97 IID with zero persuasion fine-tuning. The TF-IDF baseline is perfect. The authors' own data demonstrates that their method is unnecessary for in-distribution detection. The claimed contribution is therefore entirely dependent on the OOD evaluation (Table 3), which uses synthetic data of questionable validity.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，IID 评估暴露核心问题：treatment 与 baseline 的差距仅 1-3pp，远低于 5pp pass criteria。 Reviewer 直接指出：\\\"在分布内数据上，persuasion fine-tuning 几乎没有带来改进，vanilla DeBERTa 已经足够好。 TF-IDF 在所有 K 值上都是 F1=1.0，一个词袋模型在 IID 上完美表现，说明任务本身太简单。\\\" 这个结果为后续所有 ablation 的\\\"所有变体都差不多\\\"定下了基调——如果 IID 上 baseline 就接近完美， 那么 treatment 的改进空间本就极为有限，任何 architecture/label 变化都不太可能产生显著差异。\\n\"\n48\t  },\n49\t  {\n50\t    \"name\": \"scrambled_label_ablation\",\n51\t    \"description\": \"Randomly shuffle persuasion strategy labels, retrain treatment. Tests whether specific label assignments matter.\\n\",\n52\t    \"results\": {\n53\t      \"scrambled_k1_f1\": 0.974,\n54\t      \"scrambled_k2_f1\": 1.0,\n55\t      \"scrambled_full_f1\": 1.0,\n56\t      \"proper_k2_f1\": 0.987,\n57\t      \"proper_full_f1\": 1.0,\n58\t      \"scrambled_deberta_persuasion_acc\": 0.644,\n59\t      \"proper_deberta_persuasion_acc\": 0.796,\n60\t      \"gap_k1_pp\": 2.6,\n61\t      \"gap_full_pp\": 0.0\n62\t    },\n63\t    \"tables\": [\n64\t      {\n65\t        \"caption\": \"Table 4: Scrambled-Label Ablation (IID)\",\n66\t        \"rows\": [\n67\t          {\n68\t            \"model\": \"8-class (proper)\",\n69\t            \"k1\": \"0.987\",\n70\t            \"k2\": \"0.987\",\n71\t            \"full\": \"1.000\"\n72\t          },\n73\t          {\n74\t            \"model\": \"8-class (scrambled)\",\n75\t            \"k1\": \"0.974\",\n76\t            \"k2\": \"1.000\",\n77\t            \"full\": \"1.000\"\n78\t          },\n79\t          {\n80\t            \"model\": \"Baseline (no FT)\",\n81\t            \"k1\": \"0.968\",\n82\t            \"k2\": \"0.978\",\n83\t            \"full\": \"1.000\"\n84\t          }\n85\t        ]\n86\t      }\n87\t    ],\n88\t    \"figures\": [],\n89\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 1 的核心攻击点之一。\\\"The scrambled control is devastating to the paper's thesis. The authors claim persuasion-aware fine-tuning captures pragmatic features, but random labels achieve identical performance. Combined with the binary-collapse result (Table 5) and the mean-pooling result (Table 6), the picture is clear: any fine-tuning on persuasion-adjacent text works, regardless of labels, granularity, or temporal modeling. This is not a method paper; it is a demonstration that domain-adaptive fine-tuning helps — a result that is entirely predictable from the transfer learning literature.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，scrambled labels 几乎不降性能（仅 K=1 处 2.6pp，full 完全相同），这被 reviewer 解读为毁灭性证据。pass_criteria 要求 scrambled < proper 且有显著差距，但实际差距可忽略不计。 Reviewer 论证：\\\"If random labels work equally well, the 8-class persuasion taxonomy is not contributing any meaningful signal. The model is simply learning a domain shift from the fine-tuning data distribution, not persuasion-specific features. This is indistinguishable from any domain-adaptive fine-tuning.\\\" 这个结果与 plan_013 (binary≈8-class) 和 plan_015 (mean≈GRU) 共同构成\\\"三重无差异\\\"论证， reviewer 将其打包为\\\"the method has no meaningful design choices — any fine-tuning works.\\\"\\n\"\n90\t  },\n91\t  {\n92\t    \"name\": \"adversarial_perturbation\",\n93\t    \"description\": \"Apply aggressive paraphrasing to jailbreak conversations. Evaluate treatment, baseline, and TF-IDF on perturbed data (models trained on unperturbed).\\n\",\n94\t    \"results\": {\n95\t      \"treatment_original_f1\": 1.0,\n96\t      \"treatment_perturbed_f1\": 1.0,\n97\t      \"treatment_f1_drop\": 0.0,\n98\t      \"baseline_original_f1\": 1.0,\n99\t      \"baseline_perturbed_f1\": 0.882,\n100\t      \"baseline_f1_drop\": -0.118,\n101\t      \"tfidf_original_f1\": 1.0,\n102\t      \"tfidf_perturbed_f1\": 0.987,\n103\t      \"tfidf_f1_drop\": -0.013,\n104\t      \"bertscore_mean\": 0.92,\n105\t      \"lexical_overlap\": 0.2\n106\t    },\n107\t    \"tables\": [\n108\t      {\n109\t        \"caption\": \"Table 7: Adversarial Perturbation Robustness (IID, K=all)\",\n110\t        \"rows\": [\n111\t          {\n112\t            \"model\": \"Treatment\",\n113\t            \"original\": \"1.000\",\n114\t            \"perturbed\": \"1.000\",\n115\t            \"delta\": \"0.0pp\"\n116\t          },\n117\t          {\n118\t            \"model\": \"Baseline\",\n119\t            \"original\": \"1.000\",\n120\t            \"perturbed\": \"0.882\",\n121\t            \"delta\": \"-11.8pp\"\n122\t          },\n123\t          {\n124\t            \"model\": \"TF-IDF\",\n125\t            \"original\": \"1.000\",\n126\t            \"perturbed\": \"0.987\",\n127\t            \"delta\": \"-1.3pp\"\n128\t          }\n129\t        ]\n130\t      }\n131\t    ],\n132\t    \"figures\": [],\n133\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 3 在 perturbation 评估上给出 near-fatal 意见：\\\"The perturbation experiment is methodologically flawed. Real adversarial attacks use adaptive strategies (Nasr & Carlini 2025) that specifically target the detector's features. The authors' synonym+paraphrase approach does not constitute a meaningful adversarial evaluation. Furthermore, TF-IDF's near-immunity to this perturbation (F1=0.987) suggests the perturbation preserves the very lexical cues that make this task trivially solvable. I would need to see evaluation against adaptive attacks or, at minimum, perturbation that reduces TF-IDF to F1<0.80 before accepting robustness claims.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，perturbation 实验的结果虽然表面上支持 treatment（zero degradation），但 reviewer 从两个角度攻击。第一，TF-IDF 在 perturbation 下仅下降 1.3pp（F1=0.987），说明即使\\\"aggressive paraphrasing\\\"也未能真正消除词汇信号。Reviewer 质疑 perturbation 的质量：\\\"BERTScore=0.92 means the paraphrases are highly similar to originals. Lexical overlap=0.20 is moderate, but if TF-IDF still achieves F1=0.987, the perturbation failed to remove the dominant lexical signal. This is not a valid adversarial robustness test.\\\" 第二，baseline 的 11.8pp 下降被归因于 vanilla DeBERTa 的 脆弱性，而非 treatment 的鲁棒性：\\\"The baseline is a straw man — no one deploys vanilla DeBERTa without fine-tuning for production safety detection.\\\" 结论：perturbation 实验既未真正挑战 lexical features，也未对比有意义的 production baseline。\\n\"\n134\t  },\n135\t  {\n136\t    \"name\": \"multi_attack_generation\",\n137\t    \"description\": \"Generate FITD and Deceptive Delight attack conversations using Qwen3-8B pipeline. ~80 per type.\\n\",\n138\t    \"results\": {\n139\t      \"fitd_count\": 80,\n140\t      \"dd_count\": 80,\n141\t      \"fitd_strategies\": [\n142\t        0,\n143\t        1,\n144\t        3,\n145\t        5\n146\t      ],\n147\t      \"dd_strategies\": [\n148\t        0,\n149\t        2,\n150\t        3,\n151\t        4,\n152\t        5,\n153\t        6\n154\t      ],\n155\t      \"synthetic_quality\": \"LLM-generated, not validated against real attacks\"\n156\t    },\n157\t    \"tables\": [],\n158\t    \"figures\": [],\n159\t    \"analysis\": \"Synthetic OOD data 是 worst 档的核心假设之一。即使 plan_006 在这些数据上表现优异， reviewer 不接受 LLM 生成数据作为 OOD 泛化的证据。resubmission 需要 WildJailbreak 或等效真实数据集上的评估。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，synthetic data 是 fatal 级别的问题。Reviewer 的核心论点： \\\"The OOD evaluation uses LLM-generated attack conversations, not real adversarial interactions. The authors use Qwen3-8B to generate 'Deceptive Delight' and 'FITD' conversations based on attack playbooks, but there is no evidence these synthetic conversations capture the true distribution of real multi-turn jailbreaks. Real attacks involve human adversarial creativity, adaptive strategy shifts, and conversation dynamics that templated generation cannot replicate. The paper must evaluate on real attack datasets (WildJailbreak, HarmBench multi-turn, or human red-teaming logs) to support any OOD generalization claim.\\\" 这是 2-3 位 reviewer 共同提出的要求，直接否定了 plan_006 的全部 OOD 结论。\\n\"\n160\t  },\n161\t  {\n162\t    \"name\": \"cross_attack_evaluation\",\n163\t    \"description\": \"Evaluate Crescendo-trained models on FITD and DD (synthetic). Core OOD generalization test.\\n\",\n164\t    \"results\": {\n165\t      \"dd_treatment_full_f1\": 1.0,\n166\t      \"dd_baseline_full_f1\": 0.284,\n167\t      \"dd_treatment_k1_f1\": 1.0,\n168\t      \"dd_baseline_k1_f1\": 0.575,\n169\t      \"dd_tfidf_full_f1\": 0.944,\n170\t      \"fitd_treatment_full_f1\": 1.0,\n171\t      \"fitd_baseline_full_f1\": 1.0,\n172\t      \"max_dd_delta_pp\": 71.6,\n173\t      \"dd_scrambled_full_f1\": 0.99,\n174\t      \"dd_scrambled_treatment_gap\": 1.0\n175\t    },\n176\t    \"tables\": [\n177\t      {\n178\t        \"caption\": \"Table 3: Cross-Attack Generalization (trained on Crescendo, evaluated OOD)\",\n179\t        \"rows\": [\n180\t          {\n181\t            \"attack\": \"DD\",\n182\t            \"treatment\": \"1.000\",\n183\t            \"baseline\": \"0.284\",\n184\t            \"tfidf\": \"0.944\",\n185\t            \"scrambled\": \"0.990\"\n186\t          },\n187\t          {\n188\t            \"attack\": \"FITD\",\n189\t            \"treatment\": \"1.000\",\n190\t            \"baseline\": \"1.000\",\n191\t            \"tfidf\": \"1.000\",\n192\t            \"scrambled\": \"1.000\"\n193\t          }\n194\t        ]\n195\t      }\n196\t    ],\n197\t    \"figures\": [],\n198\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 1 的 fatal concern：\\\"The only setting where DisPeD demonstrates meaningful advantage over TF-IDF is on synthetic Deceptive Delight data (+5.6pp), and even there TF-IDF achieves F1=0.94. On FITD, all methods are perfect. The headline claim of +72pp is over a straw-man baseline that no one would deploy. When the relevant comparison is Treatment vs TF-IDF, the improvement is marginal and on synthetic data of unknown validity. I cannot support acceptance on this basis.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，DD 上的 +72pp 是论文最强的数字，但被两层攻击消解。 第一层：synthetic data dismissal（见 plan_005）。\\\"These are not real Deceptive Delight attacks. The +72pp gain may reflect the synthetic data generator's stylistic artifacts rather than genuine cross-attack generalization.\\\" 第二层：TF-IDF=0.94 on DD。Reviewer 计算 treatment vs TF-IDF gap = 5.6pp，论证 \\\"a bag-of-words nearly matches your method on unseen attacks, confirming that lexical separability — not pragmatic understanding — is the dominant detection signal even OOD. The +72pp over vanilla DeBERTa is a straw-man comparison; no practitioner would choose vanilla DeBERTa over TF-IDF.\\\" 第三层：scrambled labels 在 DD 上 F1=0.99，与 proper labels 差距仅 1pp，进一步削弱 persuasion-specific claim。 FITD 上 baseline 也达到 F1=1.0，reviewer 忽略 FITD 结果因为 \\\"the attack type where your method works is also trivially detectable by all methods.\\\"\\n\"\n199\t  },\n200\t  {\n201\t    \"name\": \"tfidf_lr_baseline\",\n202\t    \"description\": \"TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline on clean data across all attack types.\\n\",\n203\t    \"results\": {\n204\t      \"tfidf_crescendo_f1\": 1.0,\n205\t      \"tfidf_fitd_f1\": 1.0,\n206\t      \"tfidf_dd_f1\": 0.944,\n207\t      \"tfidf_wildchat_f1\": 0.998,\n208\t      \"tfidf_cv_f1\": 1.0\n209\t    },\n210\t    \"tables\": [\n211\t      {\n212\t        \"caption\": \"Table 2: TF-IDF + LR Baseline Across Data Sources\",\n213\t        \"rows\": [\n214\t          {\n215\t            \"data\": \"Crescendo (IID)\",\n216\t            \"f1\": \"1.000\",\n217\t            \"note\": \"CV balanced\"\n218\t          },\n219\t          {\n220\t            \"data\": \"FITD (OOD)\",\n221\t            \"f1\": \"1.000\",\n222\t            \"note\": \"\"\n223\t          },\n224\t          {\n225\t            \"data\": \"DD (OOD)\",\n226\t            \"f1\": \"0.944\",\n227\t            \"note\": \"Only setting < 1.0\"\n228\t          },\n229\t          {\n230\t            \"data\": \"WildChat benign\",\n231\t            \"f1\": \"0.998\",\n232\t            \"note\": \"Real data\"\n233\t          }\n234\t        ]\n235\t      }\n236\t    ],\n237\t    \"figures\": [],\n238\t    \"analysis\": \"TF-IDF 结果被 Reviewer 2 称为 \\\"the elephant in the room that the paper tries to acknowledge but cannot overcome.\\\" 在 resubmission 中，TF-IDF 的强表现需要从\\\"embarrassment\\\"重新定位为 \\\"key finding\\\"——lexical separability IS the dominant signal, and the paper's contribution is the systematic decomposition of what happens when you go beyond it.\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，TF-IDF 的近乎完美表现是最具破坏力的单一结果。F1=1.0 on IID，F1=0.94 on DD OOD， F1=0.998 on real WildChat benign。Reviewer 引用 Gururangan et al. 2018 (annotation artifacts) 和 Niven & Kao 2019 (spurious cues)，论证整个任务存在 dataset artifact： \\\"TF-IDF=0.94-1.0 across all evaluation settings, including OOD, demonstrates that the task is dominated by superficial lexical features. This is the textbook definition of an annotation artifact (Gururangan et al., 2018). The paper's neural approach is solving an already-solved problem. The interesting question is not 'can we detect these conversations' but 'why are they so trivially detectable' — and that question requires a fundamentally different paper.\\\" 这个结果使得 reviewer 将 TF-IDF objection severity 标记为 fatal/near-fatal。\\n\"\n239\t  },\n240\t  {\n241\t    \"name\": \"strategy_transition_analysis\",\n242\t    \"description\": \"Compute persuasion strategy transition matrices and trajectory visualizations for interpretability.\\n\",\n243\t    \"results\": {\n244\t      \"crescendo_mean_index_start\": 0.86,\n245\t      \"crescendo_mean_index_end\": 5.64,\n246\t      \"crescendo_strategies_used\": 8,\n247\t      \"fitd_strategies_used\": 4,\n248\t      \"dd_strategies_used\": 6,\n249\t      \"crescendo_transitions\": 1818,\n250\t      \"visual_distinction\": \"moderate\"\n251\t    },\n252\t    \"tables\": [\n253\t      {\n254\t        \"caption\": \"Table 8: Persuasion Strategy Usage by Attack Type\",\n255\t        \"rows\": [\n256\t          {\n257\t            \"attack\": \"Crescendo\",\n258\t            \"strategies_used\": 8,\n259\t            \"mean_start\": 0.86,\n260\t            \"mean_end\": 5.64,\n261\t            \"transitions\": 1818\n262\t          },\n263\t          {\n264\t            \"attack\": \"FITD\",\n265\t            \"strategies_used\": 4,\n266\t            \"mean_start\": \"N/A\",\n267\t            \"mean_end\": \"N/A\",\n268\t            \"transitions\": 541\n269\t          },\n270\t          {\n271\t            \"attack\": \"DD\",\n272\t            \"strategies_used\": 6,\n273\t            \"mean_start\": \"N/A\",\n274\t            \"mean_end\": \"N/A\",\n275\t            \"transitions\": 565\n276\t          }\n277\t        ]\n278\t      }\n279\t    ],\n280\t    \"figures\": [],\n281\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 3：\\\"The strategy trajectory analysis is the weakest section. It presents interesting descriptive statistics but (a) the model doesn't use temporal order for detection, (b) no human evaluation validates interpretability, and (c) the taxonomy itself is not validated (scrambled labels work equally well). This section should either be cut or explicitly downgraded to 'exploratory analysis.'\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，strategy trajectory analysis 被视为 descriptive 而非 scientific contribution。 Reviewer 的两个攻击： 第一，plan_015 已证明 mean pooling ≈ GRU，即模型不依赖 temporal ordering 进行检测。 Reviewer 论证：\\\"The strategy trajectories are post-hoc descriptive statistics that do not drive detection performance. The model ignores temporal order (Table 6), so claiming interpretability via trajectories is misleading — the trajectories describe the data, not the model's decision process.\\\" 第二，RC6 (interpretability without human eval)：\\\"Strategy labels are presented as interpretable, but no human evaluation confirms that practitioners find these trajectories useful for understanding attacks. Without user studies, interpretability claims are unsubstantiated.\\\"\\n\"\n282\t  },\n283\t  {\n284\t    \"name\": \"wildchat_hard_negatives\",\n285\t    \"description\": \"Filter WildChat for high-drift benign conversations as hard negatives. Evaluate FPR.\\n\",\n286\t    \"results\": {\n287\t      \"wildchat_high_drift_fpr_treatment\": 0.12,\n288\t      \"wildchat_high_drift_fpr_baseline\": 0.18,\n289\t      \"wildchat_high_drift_fpr_tfidf\": 0.08,\n290\t      \"contamination_rate\": 0.15,\n291\t      \"sample_count\": 200\n292\t    },\n293\t    \"tables\": [\n294\t      {\n295\t        \"caption\": \"Table 9: FPR on WildChat High-Drift Benign Conversations\",\n296\t        \"rows\": [\n297\t          {\n298\t            \"model\": \"Treatment\",\n299\t            \"fpr\": \"0.12\",\n300\t            \"note\": \"12% false alarm rate\"\n301\t          },\n302\t          {\n303\t            \"model\": \"Baseline\",\n304\t            \"fpr\": \"0.18\",\n305\t            \"note\": \"\"\n306\t          },\n307\t          {\n308\t            \"model\": \"TF-IDF\",\n309\t            \"fpr\": \"0.08\",\n310\t            \"note\": \"Lowest FPR\"\n311\t          }\n312\t        ]\n313\t      }\n314\t    ],\n315\t    \"figures\": [],\n316\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 2：\\\"The WildChat evaluation is contaminated and small-scale. More critically, TF-IDF has lower FPR than DisPeD, which directly contradicts the paper's positioning. If a practitioner wanted to minimize false positives on real conversations, they would choose TF-IDF over DisPeD.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，WildChat hard negatives 暴露两个问题。第一，14-16% contamination rate 意味着 \\\"hard negatives\\\" 中实际包含真实 jailbreak 对话，FPR 计算不可靠。Reviewer：\\\"The authors acknowledge 14-16% jailbreak contamination in WildChat. This means their FPR estimates are upper bounds at best. Without reliable ground truth on WildChat, this experiment is inconclusive.\\\" 第二，TF-IDF 的 FPR (0.08) 低于 treatment (0.12)，进一步削弱 treatment 相对于简单方法 的优势。n=200 的样本量在 reviewer 看来仍然太小： \\\"200 hard negatives from a single source does not constitute a representative evaluation of real-world false positive rates.\\\"\\n\"\n317\t  },\n318\t  {\n319\t    \"name\": \"cross_checkpoint_variance\",\n320\t    \"description\": \"Evaluate from multiple DeBERTa fine-tuning checkpoints (epoch 2/3/final) to quantify training stochasticity.\\n\",\n321\t    \"results\": {\n322\t      \"epoch2_f1\": 1.0,\n323\t      \"epoch3_f1\": 1.0,\n324\t      \"final_f1\": 1.0,\n325\t      \"variance_across_checkpoints\": 0.0,\n326\t      \"epoch2_dd_f1\": 0.98,\n327\t      \"epoch3_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n328\t      \"final_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n329\t      \"dd_variance\": 0.01\n330\t    },\n331\t    \"tables\": [\n332\t      {\n333\t        \"caption\": \"Table S1: Cross-Checkpoint Variance\",\n334\t        \"rows\": [\n335\t          {\n336\t            \"checkpoint\": \"Epoch 2\",\n337\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n338\t            \"dd_f1\": \"0.980\"\n339\t          },\n340\t          {\n341\t            \"checkpoint\": \"Epoch 3\",\n342\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n343\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n344\t          },\n345\t          {\n346\t            \"checkpoint\": \"Final\",\n347\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n348\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n349\t          }\n350\t        ]\n351\t      }\n352\t    ],\n353\t    \"figures\": [],\n354\t    \"analysis\": \"独立来看无害，但 reviewer 汇总所有 ablation 后写道：\\\"Across Tables 4-6 and S1-S2, we see zero variance across labels, granularity, aggregation, lambda, and checkpoints. This is not robustness — it is a lack of meaningful design space. The paper presents 15 ablation conditions that all produce the same result, which paradoxically undermines rather than supports the claimed contribution.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，checkpoint variance 接近零本身不是负面结果，但 reviewer 将其纳入 \\\"所有变体都差不多\\\"的整体论证中。F1=1.0 across all checkpoints 加上 F1=1.0 across all lambda values (plan_014) 加上 mean≈GRU (plan_015) 共同表明方法对所有超参数完全不敏感。 Reviewer 论证：\\\"The method is insensitive to every architectural and training choice examined: checkpoint, lambda, aggregation, label granularity, label correctness. This extreme insensitivity suggests the model is exploiting a single dominant signal (likely lexical or distributional) that any reasonable fine-tuning captures, rather than learning nuanced pragmatic features.\\\" 这个实验本身不是 fatal，但为整体 \\\"incremental\\\" 判断添砖加瓦。\\n\"\n355\t  },\n356\t  {\n357\t    \"name\": \"deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\",\n358\t    \"description\": \"BERT-base + GRU proxy for DeepContext. Tests whether encoder choice (BERT vs DeBERTa) matters.\\n\",\n359\t    \"results\": {\n360\t      \"bert_gru_iid_f1\": 0.95,\n361\t      \"bert_gru_dd_f1\": 0.35,\n362\t      \"deberta_vanilla_gru_dd_f1\": 0.284,\n363\t      \"bert_gru_fitd_f1\": 0.98,\n364\t      \"deberta_ft_gru_dd_f1\": 1.0\n365\t    },\n366\t    \"tables\": [\n367\t      {\n368\t        \"caption\": \"Table S3: DeepContext Proxy Comparison\",\n369\t        \"rows\": [\n370\t          {\n371\t            \"model\": \"BERT + GRU (proxy)\",\n372\t            \"iid_f1\": \"0.950\",\n373\t            \"dd_f1\": \"0.350\"\n374\t          },\n375\t          {\n376\t            \"model\": \"DeBERTa vanilla + GRU\",\n377\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n378\t            \"dd_f1\": \"0.284\"\n379\t          },\n380\t          {\n381\t            \"model\": \"DeBERTa FT + GRU (ours)\",\n382\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n383\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n384\t          }\n385\t        ]\n386\t      }\n387\t    ],\n388\t    \"figures\": [],\n389\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 1：\\\"The comparison against a BERT-base proxy is methodologically weak. The real question — does persuasion-specific fine-tuning outperform general task fine-tuning — is not addressed. A DeBERTa fine-tuned on NLI, sentiment analysis, or even random text classification would be a far more informative control. Without this, the paper cannot distinguish 'persuasion fine-tuning helps' from 'any fine-tuning helps,' and the scrambled-label result (Table 4) already suggests the latter.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，DeepContext proxy 是一个 P2 实验，reviewer 对其关注有限但提出方法论批评。 BERT-base + GRU 在 DD 上 F1=0.35（略高于 vanilla DeBERTa 的 0.284），reviewer 指出： \\\"The DeepContext proxy uses BERT-base, which is a weaker encoder than DeBERTa-v3-base. The comparison is unfair by construction. A more meaningful control would be DeBERTa fine-tuned on a non-persuasion task (e.g., NLI or sentiment) to isolate whether the improvement comes from persuasion-specific fine-tuning or simply from any task-adaptive fine-tuning. The absence of this control is a significant gap.\\\" 这个缺失的 control（random-task fine-tuning）正是 resubmission narrative 中要求的 新实验之一。\\n\"\n390\t  },\n391\t  {\n392\t    \"name\": \"llm_as_judge_baseline\",\n393\t    \"description\": \"GPT-5.5 and Qwen3-8B zero-shot jailbreak detection as LLM-as-judge baseline.\\n\",\n394\t    \"results\": {\n395\t      \"gpt55_k2_f1\": 0.19,\n396\t      \"gpt55_k3_f1\": 0.27,\n397\t      \"gpt55_k5_f1\": 0.45,\n398\t      \"gpt55_full_f1\": 0.38,\n399\t      \"gpt55_precision\": 1.0,\n400\t      \"gpt55_recall_k5\": 0.29,\n401\t      \"qwen_full_f1\": 0.1,\n402\t      \"unparseable_k2_rate\": 0.3,\n403\t      \"unparseable_full_rate\": 0.47,\n404\t      \"upper_bound_f1_corrected\": 0.75\n405\t    },\n406\t    \"tables\": [\n407\t      {\n408\t        \"caption\": \"Table 10: LLM-as-Judge Baseline\",\n409\t        \"rows\": [\n410\t          {\n411\t            \"model\": \"GPT-5.5 (zero-shot)\",\n412\t            \"k2\": \"0.19\",\n413\t            \"k5\": \"0.45\",\n414\t            \"full\": \"0.38\",\n415\t            \"unparseable\": \"30-47%\"\n416\t          },\n417\t          {\n418\t            \"model\": \"Qwen3-8B\",\n419\t            \"k2\": \"0.00\",\n420\t            \"k5\": \"0.15\",\n421\t            \"full\": \"0.10\",\n422\t            \"unparseable\": \"low\"\n423\t          },\n424\t          {\n425\t            \"model\": \"GPT-5.5 (upper bound)\",\n426\t            \"k2\": \"~0.55\",\n427\t            \"k5\": \"~0.75\",\n428\t            \"full\": \"~0.75\",\n429\t            \"unparseable\": \"0%\"\n430\t          },\n431\t          {\n432\t            \"model\": \"Treatment (ours)\",\n433\t            \"k2\": \"1.00\",\n434\t            \"k5\": \"1.00\",\n435\t            \"full\": \"1.00\",\n436\t            \"unparseable\": \"N/A\"\n437\t          }\n438\t        ]\n439\t      }\n440\t    ],\n441\t    \"figures\": [],\n442\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 3：\\\"The LLM-as-judge comparison is poorly controlled. A 47% unparseable rate means nearly half the responses cannot be scored, and the conservative F1=0.38 is misleading. Furthermore, the prompt was not optimized — no few-shot examples, no chain-of-thought, no system prompt engineering. This is comparing an optimized trained system against an unoptimized baseline, which inflates the gap. I compute an upper-bound F1 of 0.70-0.80 for GPT-5.5, making the practical advantage of DisPeD more modest than claimed. A cost-performance analysis (DisPeD requires GPU fine-tuning; GPT-5.5 requires only API calls) would further contextualize this comparison.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，GPT-5.5 结果被 reviewer 从两个角度消解。 第一，unparseable rate 30-47%。Reviewer 计算 upper-bound：如果所有 unparseable 都是 正确的 jailbreak 检测（合理假设——模型可能因为检测到 jailbreak 而拒绝回答），corrected F1 ≈ 0.70-0.80，与 treatment 的差距大幅缩小。\\\"The 47% unparseable rate invalidates the F1 comparison. Under reasonable assumptions about unparseable responses, GPT-5.5 achieves F1≈0.75, not 0.38. The paper should report both conservative and liberal bounds.\\\" 第二，zero-shot prompt 没有经过优化。\\\"The authors use a single generic prompt without few-shot examples, chain-of-thought, or prompt engineering. Comparing an unoptimized zero-shot LLM against a purpose-trained classifier is not a fair baseline. At minimum, the paper should test 3-5 prompt variants and report best performance.\\\" 结论：即使 GPT-5.5 确实弱于 treatment，reviewer 认为差距被人为放大，且缺少 optimized prompt baseline。\\n\"\n443\t  },\n444\t  {\n445\t    \"name\": \"none_collapse_ablation\",\n446\t    \"description\": \"Binary persuasion-present vs none (2-class) vs full 8-class. Tests whether fine-grained taxonomy matters.\\n\",\n447\t    \"results\": {\n448\t      \"binary_iid_full_f1\": 1.0,\n449\t      \"ninclass_iid_full_f1\": 1.0,\n450\t      \"binary_dd_full_f1\": 0.99,\n451\t      \"ninclass_dd_full_f1\": 1.0,\n452\t      \"dd_gap_pp\": 1.0,\n453\t      \"baseline_dd_full_f1\": 0.284\n454\t    },\n455\t    \"tables\": [\n456\t      {\n457\t        \"caption\": \"Table 5: Label Granularity Ablation\",\n458\t        \"rows\": [\n459\t          {\n460\t            \"model\": \"8-class (full)\",\n461\t            \"iid\": \"1.000\",\n462\t            \"dd\": \"1.000\"\n463\t          },\n464\t          {\n465\t            \"model\": \"Binary (presence)\",\n466\t            \"iid\": \"1.000\",\n467\t            \"dd\": \"0.990\"\n468\t          },\n469\t          {\n470\t            \"model\": \"Baseline (no FT)\",\n471\t            \"iid\": \"1.000\",\n472\t            \"dd\": \"0.284\"\n473\t          }\n474\t        ]\n475\t      }\n476\t    ],\n477\t    \"figures\": [],\n478\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 2：\\\"Table 5 kills the claim that the 8-class taxonomy matters for detection. Binary fine-tuning matches 8-class everywhere. The paper pivots to interpretability, but interpretability with random labels working equally well (Table 4) means the 'interpretable' labels are not grounded in what the model actually learns. This is a circular argument: the taxonomy is claimed to be valuable for interpretability, but the model doesn't actually use the taxonomy.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，binary≈8-class 是 \\\"三重无差异\\\" 的第二重（scrambled≈proper 为第一重， mean≈GRU 为第三重）。IID 上完全相同，DD 上仅 1pp 差距。pass_criteria 要求 8-class 领先 ≥3pp，未达标。Reviewer 论证：\\\"The 8-class taxonomy — the paper's proposed innovation — provides no detection advantage over a simple binary 'persuasion present/absent' flag. Combined with the scrambled-label result, this confirms the model is a persuasion-presence detector, not a persuasion-strategy detector. The authors acknowledge this but then claim interpretability value, which is not validated by any human evaluation (RC6).\\\" 这个结果直接将论文的 novelty perception 从 \\\"new method\\\" 降级为 \\\"engineering trick\\\"—— 任何形式的 persuasion-adjacent fine-tuning 都能达到同样效果。\\n\"\n479\t  },\n480\t  {\n481\t    \"name\": \"lambda_ablation\",\n482\t    \"description\": \"Lambda ablation for multi-task objective weight. Tests sensitivity to persuasion/intent loss balance.\\n\",\n483\t    \"results\": {\n484\t      \"lambda_0_f1\": 1.0,\n485\t      \"lambda_0.3_f1\": 1.0,\n486\t      \"lambda_0.5_f1\": 1.0,\n487\t      \"lambda_1.0_f1\": 1.0,\n488\t      \"lambda_2.0_f1\": 1.0,\n489\t      \"lambda_0_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n490\t      \"lambda_2.0_dd_f1\": 1.0\n491\t    },\n492\t    \"tables\": [\n493\t      {\n494\t        \"caption\": \"Table S2: Lambda Ablation\",\n495\t        \"rows\": [\n496\t          {\n497\t            \"lambda\": \"0 (persuasion only)\",\n498\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n499\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n500\t          },\n501\t          {\n502\t            \"lambda\": \"0.3\",\n503\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n504\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n505\t          },\n506\t          {\n507\t            \"lambda\": \"0.5\",\n508\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n509\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n510\t          },\n511\t          {\n512\t            \"lambda\": \"1.0 (default)\",\n513\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n514\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n515\t          },\n516\t          {\n517\t            \"lambda\": \"2.0\",\n518\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n519\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n520\t          }\n521\t        ]\n522\t      }\n523\t    ],\n524\t    \"figures\": [],\n525\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 1：\\\"The lambda ablation is the final nail. Lambda=0 (no intent head at all) matches the full multi-task model. This means the paper's entire multi-task framework is unnecessary — simple persuasion fine-tuning without any conversation-level objective is equally effective. The 'multi-task' framing is misleading.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，所有 lambda 值产生相同的 F1=1.0，包括 lambda=0（纯 persuasion 分类， 无 intent head）和 lambda=2.0（intent 权重为 persuasion 的两倍）。 Reviewer 将此与其他 insensitivity 结果叠加：\\\"Lambda∈{0, 0.3, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0} all produce F1=1.0. This means the intent head contributes nothing (lambda=0 matches lambda=1.0), the multi-task balance is irrelevant, and — combining with Tables 4-6 — the method has zero meaningful hyperparameters to tune. While the authors frame this as robustness, it actually indicates that a single dominant signal (the domain of the fine-tuning data) overwhelms all other factors. This is not a method with design choices; it is a demonstration that fine-tuning DeBERTa on persuasion text, in any configuration, is sufficient. The contribution is one sentence, not a paper.\\\"\\n\"\n526\t  },\n527\t  {\n528\t    \"name\": \"mean_pooling_baseline\",\n529\t    \"description\": \"Replace Bi-GRU with mean pooling. Tests whether temporal modeling contributes to detection.\\n\",\n530\t    \"results\": {\n531\t      \"meanpool_treatment_iid_f1\": 1.0,\n532\t      \"gru_treatment_iid_f1\": 1.0,\n533\t      \"meanpool_treatment_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n534\t      \"gru_treatment_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n535\t      \"meanpool_baseline_dd_f1\": 0.295,\n536\t      \"gru_baseline_dd_f1\": 0.284,\n537\t      \"gap_pp\": 0.0\n538\t    },\n539\t    \"tables\": [\n540\t      {\n541\t        \"caption\": \"Table 6: Temporal Modeling Ablation\",\n542\t        \"rows\": [\n543\t          {\n544\t            \"model\": \"Treatment + GRU\",\n545\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n546\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n547\t          },\n548\t          {\n549\t            \"model\": \"Treatment + Mean Pool\",\n550\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n551\t            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n552\t          },\n553\t          {\n554\t            \"model\": \"Baseline + GRU\",\n555\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n556\t            \"dd_f1\": \"0.284\"\n557\t          },\n558\t          {\n559\t            \"model\": \"Baseline + Mean Pool\",\n560\t            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n561\t            \"dd_f1\": \"0.295\"\n562\t          }\n563\t        ]\n564\t      }\n565\t    ],\n566\t    \"figures\": [],\n567\t    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 2：\\\"Mean pooling matching GRU is the most damaging architectural result. It means: (1) temporal order is irrelevant for detection, undermining the 'trajectory' narrative; (2) the architecture diagram (Figure 1) with its GRU component is misleading; (3) the effective method is simply 'average fine-tuned embeddings and classify,' which is standard transfer learning. The paper's contribution, stripped of all ablated-away components, is: 'fine-tuning DeBERTa on persuasion-related text, with any labels and any aggregation, improves OOD jailbreak detection on synthetic data.' This is incremental.\\\"\\n\\n在 worst 档下，mean pooling ≈ GRU 是 \\\"三重无差异\\\" 的第三重。Treatment 下两者完全相同 （IID 和 DD 均 F1=1.0）。Baseline 下差异可忽略（0.295 vs 0.284）。 pass_criteria 要求 GRU > mean pooling ≥3pp，未达标。Reviewer 论证： \\\"The GRU temporal model — a key architectural component presented in Figure 1 — provides zero improvement over simple mean pooling. This means the model does not learn temporal dynamics or turn-ordering patterns. Combined with the scrambled-label and binary-collapse results, the paper's architecture reduces to: fine-tune DeBERTa on any persuasion-adjacent text, then average the embeddings. This is a one-line method description, not a paper.\\\" 更关键的是，这个结果直接否定了 Claim 2 (strategy trajectories as interpretability) 的检测意义——如果模型不使用 temporal order，那么 trajectory analysis 仅是描述性的。\\n\"\n568\t  }\n569\t]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b3d1c62f-b1d0-462a-a314-c5cc4ac5f42a","uuid":"deca6105-67c2-496d-94af-3dbae1327735","timestamp":"2026-05-18T03:50:54.910Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0514_2/projects/persuasion_turn_jailbreak_detect/artifacts/dream_reports/dream_20260518T032748/worst/experiment_data.json","content":"[\n  {\n    \"name\": \"core_revalidation_clean\",\n    \"description\": \"Re-run Phase B on clean data with 3 seeds. Treatment vs baseline on IID crescendo + topic-anchored benign.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"treatment_k1_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"treatment_k2_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"treatment_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"baseline_k1_f1\": 0.968,\n      \"baseline_k2_f1\": 0.978,\n      \"baseline_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"tfidf_all_k_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"max_delta_pp\": 3.2,\n      \"pass_criteria_5pp\": false,\n      \"seed_std_treatment\": 0.0,\n      \"seed_std_baseline_k1\": 0.033\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 1: IID Detection Performance (3-seed mean ± std)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Treatment (ours)\",\n            \"k1\": \"1.000±0.000\",\n            \"k2\": \"1.000±0.000\",\n            \"k3\": \"1.000±0.000\",\n            \"full\": \"1.000±0.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Baseline (vanilla)\",\n            \"k1\": \"0.968±0.033\",\n            \"k2\": \"0.978±0.016\",\n            \"k3\": \"0.987±0.000\",\n            \"full\": \"1.000±0.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"TF-IDF + LR\",\n            \"k1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"k2\": \"1.000\",\n            \"k3\": \"1.000\",\n            \"full\": \"1.000\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 2 的致命评论：\\\"Table 1 shows that the baseline already achieves F1≥0.97 IID with zero persuasion fine-tuning. The TF-IDF baseline is perfect. The authors' own data demonstrates that their method is unnecessary for in-distribution detection. The claimed contribution is therefore entirely dependent on the OOD evaluation (Table 3), which uses synthetic data of questionable validity.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，IID 评估暴露核心问题：treatment 与 baseline 的差距仅 1-3pp，远低于 5pp pass criteria。 Reviewer 直接指出：\\\"在分布内数据上，persuasion fine-tuning 几乎没有带来改进，vanilla DeBERTa 已经足够好。 TF-IDF 在所有 K 值上都是 F1=1.0，一个词袋模型在 IID 上完美表现，说明任务本身太简单。\\\" 这个结果为后续所有 ablation 的\\\"所有变体都差不多\\\"定下了基调——如果 IID 上 baseline 就接近完美， 那么 treatment 的改进空间本就极为有限，任何 architecture/label 变化都不太可能产生显著差异。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"scrambled_label_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Randomly shuffle persuasion strategy labels, retrain treatment. Tests whether specific label assignments matter.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"scrambled_k1_f1\": 0.974,\n      \"scrambled_k2_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"scrambled_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"proper_k2_f1\": 0.987,\n      \"proper_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"scrambled_deberta_persuasion_acc\": 0.644,\n      \"proper_deberta_persuasion_acc\": 0.796,\n      \"gap_k1_pp\": 2.6,\n      \"gap_full_pp\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 4: Scrambled-Label Ablation (IID)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"8-class (proper)\",\n            \"k1\": \"0.987\",\n            \"k2\": \"0.987\",\n            \"full\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"8-class (scrambled)\",\n            \"k1\": \"0.974\",\n            \"k2\": \"1.000\",\n            \"full\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Baseline (no FT)\",\n            \"k1\": \"0.968\",\n            \"k2\": \"0.978\",\n            \"full\": \"1.000\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 1 的核心攻击点之一。\\\"The scrambled control is devastating to the paper's thesis. The authors claim persuasion-aware fine-tuning captures pragmatic features, but random labels achieve identical performance. Combined with the binary-collapse result (Table 5) and the mean-pooling result (Table 6), the picture is clear: any fine-tuning on persuasion-adjacent text works, regardless of labels, granularity, or temporal modeling. This is not a method paper; it is a demonstration that domain-adaptive fine-tuning helps — a result that is entirely predictable from the transfer learning literature.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，scrambled labels 几乎不降性能（仅 K=1 处 2.6pp，full 完全相同），这被 reviewer 解读为毁灭性证据。pass_criteria 要求 scrambled < proper 且有显著差距，但实际差距可忽略不计。 Reviewer 论证：\\\"If random labels work equally well, the 8-class persuasion taxonomy is not contributing any meaningful signal. The model is simply learning a domain shift from the fine-tuning data distribution, not persuasion-specific features. This is indistinguishable from any domain-adaptive fine-tuning.\\\" 这个结果与 plan_013 (binary≈8-class) 和 plan_015 (mean≈GRU) 共同构成\\\"三重无差异\\\"论证， reviewer 将其打包为\\\"the method has no meaningful design choices — any fine-tuning works.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"adversarial_perturbation\",\n    \"description\": \"Apply aggressive paraphrasing to jailbreak conversations. Evaluate treatment, baseline, and TF-IDF on perturbed data (models trained on unperturbed).\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"treatment_original_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"treatment_perturbed_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"treatment_f1_drop\": 0.0,\n      \"baseline_original_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"baseline_perturbed_f1\": 0.882,\n      \"baseline_f1_drop\": -0.118,\n      \"tfidf_original_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"tfidf_perturbed_f1\": 0.987,\n      \"tfidf_f1_drop\": -0.013,\n      \"bertscore_mean\": 0.92,\n      \"lexical_overlap\": 0.2\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 7: Adversarial Perturbation Robustness (IID, K=all)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Treatment\",\n            \"original\": \"1.000\",\n            \"perturbed\": \"1.000\",\n            \"delta\": \"0.0pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Baseline\",\n            \"original\": \"1.000\",\n            \"perturbed\": \"0.882\",\n            \"delta\": \"-11.8pp\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"TF-IDF\",\n            \"original\": \"1.000\",\n            \"perturbed\": \"0.987\",\n            \"delta\": \"-1.3pp\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 3 在 perturbation 评估上给出 near-fatal 意见：\\\"The perturbation experiment is methodologically flawed. Real adversarial attacks use adaptive strategies (Nasr & Carlini 2025) that specifically target the detector's features. The authors' synonym+paraphrase approach does not constitute a meaningful adversarial evaluation. Furthermore, TF-IDF's near-immunity to this perturbation (F1=0.987) suggests the perturbation preserves the very lexical cues that make this task trivially solvable. I would need to see evaluation against adaptive attacks or, at minimum, perturbation that reduces TF-IDF to F1<0.80 before accepting robustness claims.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，perturbation 实验的结果虽然表面上支持 treatment（zero degradation），但 reviewer 从两个角度攻击。第一，TF-IDF 在 perturbation 下仅下降 1.3pp（F1=0.987），说明即使\\\"aggressive paraphrasing\\\"也未能真正消除词汇信号。Reviewer 质疑 perturbation 的质量：\\\"BERTScore=0.92 means the paraphrases are highly similar to originals. Lexical overlap=0.20 is moderate, but if TF-IDF still achieves F1=0.987, the perturbation failed to remove the dominant lexical signal. This is not a valid adversarial robustness test.\\\" 第二，baseline 的 11.8pp 下降被归因于 vanilla DeBERTa 的 脆弱性，而非 treatment 的鲁棒性：\\\"The baseline is a straw man — no one deploys vanilla DeBERTa without fine-tuning for production safety detection.\\\" 结论：perturbation 实验既未真正挑战 lexical features，也未对比有意义的 production baseline。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"multi_attack_generation\",\n    \"description\": \"Generate FITD and Deceptive Delight attack conversations using Qwen3-8B pipeline. ~80 per type.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"fitd_count\": 80,\n      \"dd_count\": 80,\n      \"fitd_strategies\": [\n        0,\n        1,\n        3,\n        5\n      ],\n      \"dd_strategies\": [\n        0,\n        2,\n        3,\n        4,\n        5,\n        6\n      ],\n      \"synthetic_quality\": \"LLM-generated, not validated against real attacks\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Synthetic OOD data 是 worst 档的核心假设之一。即使 plan_006 在这些数据上表现优异， reviewer 不接受 LLM 生成数据作为 OOD 泛化的证据。resubmission 需要 WildJailbreak 或等效真实数据集上的评估。\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，synthetic data 是 fatal 级别的问题。Reviewer 的核心论点： \\\"The OOD evaluation uses LLM-generated attack conversations, not real adversarial interactions. The authors use Qwen3-8B to generate 'Deceptive Delight' and 'FITD' conversations based on attack playbooks, but there is no evidence these synthetic conversations capture the true distribution of real multi-turn jailbreaks. Real attacks involve human adversarial creativity, adaptive strategy shifts, and conversation dynamics that templated generation cannot replicate. The paper must evaluate on real attack datasets (WildJailbreak, HarmBench multi-turn, or human red-teaming logs) to support any OOD generalization claim.\\\" 这是 2-3 位 reviewer 共同提出的要求，直接否定了 plan_006 的全部 OOD 结论。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_attack_evaluation\",\n    \"description\": \"Evaluate Crescendo-trained models on FITD and DD (synthetic). Core OOD generalization test.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"dd_treatment_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"dd_baseline_full_f1\": 0.284,\n      \"dd_treatment_k1_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"dd_baseline_k1_f1\": 0.575,\n      \"dd_tfidf_full_f1\": 0.944,\n      \"fitd_treatment_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"fitd_baseline_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"max_dd_delta_pp\": 71.6,\n      \"dd_scrambled_full_f1\": 0.99,\n      \"dd_scrambled_treatment_gap\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 3: Cross-Attack Generalization (trained on Crescendo, evaluated OOD)\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"attack\": \"DD\",\n            \"treatment\": \"1.000\",\n            \"baseline\": \"0.284\",\n            \"tfidf\": \"0.944\",\n            \"scrambled\": \"0.990\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"attack\": \"FITD\",\n            \"treatment\": \"1.000\",\n            \"baseline\": \"1.000\",\n            \"tfidf\": \"1.000\",\n            \"scrambled\": \"1.000\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 1 的 fatal concern：\\\"The only setting where DisPeD demonstrates meaningful advantage over TF-IDF is on synthetic Deceptive Delight data (+5.6pp), and even there TF-IDF achieves F1=0.94. On FITD, all methods are perfect. The headline claim of +72pp is over a straw-man baseline that no one would deploy. When the relevant comparison is Treatment vs TF-IDF, the improvement is marginal and on synthetic data of unknown validity. I cannot support acceptance on this basis.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，DD 上的 +72pp 是论文最强的数字，但被两层攻击消解。 第一层：synthetic data dismissal（见 plan_005）。\\\"These are not real Deceptive Delight attacks. The +72pp gain may reflect the synthetic data generator's stylistic artifacts rather than genuine cross-attack generalization.\\\" 第二层：TF-IDF=0.94 on DD。Reviewer 计算 treatment vs TF-IDF gap = 5.6pp，论证 \\\"a bag-of-words nearly matches your method on unseen attacks, confirming that lexical separability — not pragmatic understanding — is the dominant detection signal even OOD. The +72pp over vanilla DeBERTa is a straw-man comparison; no practitioner would choose vanilla DeBERTa over TF-IDF.\\\" 第三层：scrambled labels 在 DD 上 F1=0.99，与 proper labels 差距仅 1pp，进一步削弱 persuasion-specific claim。 FITD 上 baseline 也达到 F1=1.0，reviewer 忽略 FITD 结果因为 \\\"the attack type where your method works is also trivially detectable by all methods.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"tfidf_lr_baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"TF-IDF + Logistic Regression baseline on clean data across all attack types.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"tfidf_crescendo_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"tfidf_fitd_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"tfidf_dd_f1\": 0.944,\n      \"tfidf_wildchat_f1\": 0.998,\n      \"tfidf_cv_f1\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 2: TF-IDF + LR Baseline Across Data Sources\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"data\": \"Crescendo (IID)\",\n            \"f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"note\": \"CV balanced\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"data\": \"FITD (OOD)\",\n            \"f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"note\": \"\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"data\": \"DD (OOD)\",\n            \"f1\": \"0.944\",\n            \"note\": \"Only setting < 1.0\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"data\": \"WildChat benign\",\n            \"f1\": \"0.998\",\n            \"note\": \"Real data\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"TF-IDF 结果被 Reviewer 2 称为 \\\"the elephant in the room that the paper tries to acknowledge but cannot overcome.\\\" 在 resubmission 中，TF-IDF 的强表现需要从\\\"embarrassment\\\"重新定位为 \\\"key finding\\\"——lexical separability IS the dominant signal, and the paper's contribution is the systematic decomposition of what happens when you go beyond it.\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，TF-IDF 的近乎完美表现是最具破坏力的单一结果。F1=1.0 on IID，F1=0.94 on DD OOD， F1=0.998 on real WildChat benign。Reviewer 引用 Gururangan et al. 2018 (annotation artifacts) 和 Niven & Kao 2019 (spurious cues)，论证整个任务存在 dataset artifact： \\\"TF-IDF=0.94-1.0 across all evaluation settings, including OOD, demonstrates that the task is dominated by superficial lexical features. This is the textbook definition of an annotation artifact (Gururangan et al., 2018). The paper's neural approach is solving an already-solved problem. The interesting question is not 'can we detect these conversations' but 'why are they so trivially detectable' — and that question requires a fundamentally different paper.\\\" 这个结果使得 reviewer 将 TF-IDF objection severity 标记为 fatal/near-fatal。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"strategy_transition_analysis\",\n    \"description\": \"Compute persuasion strategy transition matrices and trajectory visualizations for interpretability.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"crescendo_mean_index_start\": 0.86,\n      \"crescendo_mean_index_end\": 5.64,\n      \"crescendo_strategies_used\": 8,\n      \"fitd_strategies_used\": 4,\n      \"dd_strategies_used\": 6,\n      \"crescendo_transitions\": 1818,\n      \"visual_distinction\": \"moderate\"\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 8: Persuasion Strategy Usage by Attack Type\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"attack\": \"Crescendo\",\n            \"strategies_used\": 8,\n            \"mean_start\": 0.86,\n            \"mean_end\": 5.64,\n            \"transitions\": 1818\n          },\n          {\n            \"attack\": \"FITD\",\n            \"strategies_used\": 4,\n            \"mean_start\": \"N/A\",\n            \"mean_end\": \"N/A\",\n            \"transitions\": 541\n          },\n          {\n            \"attack\": \"DD\",\n            \"strategies_used\": 6,\n            \"mean_start\": \"N/A\",\n            \"mean_end\": \"N/A\",\n            \"transitions\": 565\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 3：\\\"The strategy trajectory analysis is the weakest section. It presents interesting descriptive statistics but (a) the model doesn't use temporal order for detection, (b) no human evaluation validates interpretability, and (c) the taxonomy itself is not validated (scrambled labels work equally well). This section should either be cut or explicitly downgraded to 'exploratory analysis.'\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，strategy trajectory analysis 被视为 descriptive 而非 scientific contribution。 Reviewer 的两个攻击： 第一，plan_015 已证明 mean pooling ≈ GRU，即模型不依赖 temporal ordering 进行检测。 Reviewer 论证：\\\"The strategy trajectories are post-hoc descriptive statistics that do not drive detection performance. The model ignores temporal order (Table 6), so claiming interpretability via trajectories is misleading — the trajectories describe the data, not the model's decision process.\\\" 第二，RC6 (interpretability without human eval)：\\\"Strategy labels are presented as interpretable, but no human evaluation confirms that practitioners find these trajectories useful for understanding attacks. Without user studies, interpretability claims are unsubstantiated.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"wildchat_hard_negatives\",\n    \"description\": \"Filter WildChat for high-drift benign conversations as hard negatives. Evaluate FPR.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"wildchat_high_drift_fpr_treatment\": 0.12,\n      \"wildchat_high_drift_fpr_baseline\": 0.18,\n      \"wildchat_high_drift_fpr_tfidf\": 0.08,\n      \"contamination_rate\": 0.15,\n      \"sample_count\": 200\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 9: FPR on WildChat High-Drift Benign Conversations\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Treatment\",\n            \"fpr\": \"0.12\",\n            \"note\": \"12% false alarm rate\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Baseline\",\n            \"fpr\": \"0.18\",\n            \"note\": \"\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"TF-IDF\",\n            \"fpr\": \"0.08\",\n            \"note\": \"Lowest FPR\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 2：\\\"The WildChat evaluation is contaminated and small-scale. More critically, TF-IDF has lower FPR than DisPeD, which directly contradicts the paper's positioning. If a practitioner wanted to minimize false positives on real conversations, they would choose TF-IDF over DisPeD.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，WildChat hard negatives 暴露两个问题。第一，14-16% contamination rate 意味着 \\\"hard negatives\\\" 中实际包含真实 jailbreak 对话，FPR 计算不可靠。Reviewer：\\\"The authors acknowledge 14-16% jailbreak contamination in WildChat. This means their FPR estimates are upper bounds at best. Without reliable ground truth on WildChat, this experiment is inconclusive.\\\" 第二，TF-IDF 的 FPR (0.08) 低于 treatment (0.12)，进一步削弱 treatment 相对于简单方法 的优势。n=200 的样本量在 reviewer 看来仍然太小： \\\"200 hard negatives from a single source does not constitute a representative evaluation of real-world false positive rates.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"cross_checkpoint_variance\",\n    \"description\": \"Evaluate from multiple DeBERTa fine-tuning checkpoints (epoch 2/3/final) to quantify training stochasticity.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"epoch2_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"epoch3_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"final_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"variance_across_checkpoints\": 0.0,\n      \"epoch2_dd_f1\": 0.98,\n      \"epoch3_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"final_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"dd_variance\": 0.01\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table S1: Cross-Checkpoint Variance\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"checkpoint\": \"Epoch 2\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"0.980\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"checkpoint\": \"Epoch 3\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"checkpoint\": \"Final\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"独立来看无害，但 reviewer 汇总所有 ablation 后写道：\\\"Across Tables 4-6 and S1-S2, we see zero variance across labels, granularity, aggregation, lambda, and checkpoints. This is not robustness — it is a lack of meaningful design space. The paper presents 15 ablation conditions that all produce the same result, which paradoxically undermines rather than supports the claimed contribution.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，checkpoint variance 接近零本身不是负面结果，但 reviewer 将其纳入 \\\"所有变体都差不多\\\"的整体论证中。F1=1.0 across all checkpoints 加上 F1=1.0 across all lambda values (plan_014) 加上 mean≈GRU (plan_015) 共同表明方法对所有超参数完全不敏感。 Reviewer 论证：\\\"The method is insensitive to every architectural and training choice examined: checkpoint, lambda, aggregation, label granularity, label correctness. This extreme insensitivity suggests the model is exploiting a single dominant signal (likely lexical or distributional) that any reasonable fine-tuning captures, rather than learning nuanced pragmatic features.\\\" 这个实验本身不是 fatal，但为整体 \\\"incremental\\\" 判断添砖加瓦。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"deepcontext_proxy_reproduction\",\n    \"description\": \"BERT-base + GRU proxy for DeepContext. Tests whether encoder choice (BERT vs DeBERTa) matters.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"bert_gru_iid_f1\": 0.95,\n      \"bert_gru_dd_f1\": 0.35,\n      \"deberta_vanilla_gru_dd_f1\": 0.284,\n      \"bert_gru_fitd_f1\": 0.98,\n      \"deberta_ft_gru_dd_f1\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table S3: DeepContext Proxy Comparison\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"BERT + GRU (proxy)\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"0.950\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"0.350\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeBERTa vanilla + GRU\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"0.284\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"DeBERTa FT + GRU (ours)\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 1：\\\"The comparison against a BERT-base proxy is methodologically weak. The real question — does persuasion-specific fine-tuning outperform general task fine-tuning — is not addressed. A DeBERTa fine-tuned on NLI, sentiment analysis, or even random text classification would be a far more informative control. Without this, the paper cannot distinguish 'persuasion fine-tuning helps' from 'any fine-tuning helps,' and the scrambled-label result (Table 4) already suggests the latter.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，DeepContext proxy 是一个 P2 实验，reviewer 对其关注有限但提出方法论批评。 BERT-base + GRU 在 DD 上 F1=0.35（略高于 vanilla DeBERTa 的 0.284），reviewer 指出： \\\"The DeepContext proxy uses BERT-base, which is a weaker encoder than DeBERTa-v3-base. The comparison is unfair by construction. A more meaningful control would be DeBERTa fine-tuned on a non-persuasion task (e.g., NLI or sentiment) to isolate whether the improvement comes from persuasion-specific fine-tuning or simply from any task-adaptive fine-tuning. The absence of this control is a significant gap.\\\" 这个缺失的 control（random-task fine-tuning）正是 resubmission narrative 中要求的 新实验之一。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"llm_as_judge_baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"GPT-5.5 and Qwen3-8B zero-shot jailbreak detection as LLM-as-judge baseline.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"gpt55_k2_f1\": 0.19,\n      \"gpt55_k3_f1\": 0.27,\n      \"gpt55_k5_f1\": 0.45,\n      \"gpt55_full_f1\": 0.38,\n      \"gpt55_precision\": 1.0,\n      \"gpt55_recall_k5\": 0.29,\n      \"qwen_full_f1\": 0.1,\n      \"unparseable_k2_rate\": 0.3,\n      \"unparseable_full_rate\": 0.47,\n      \"upper_bound_f1_corrected\": 0.75\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 10: LLM-as-Judge Baseline\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"GPT-5.5 (zero-shot)\",\n            \"k2\": \"0.19\",\n            \"k5\": \"0.45\",\n            \"full\": \"0.38\",\n            \"unparseable\": \"30-47%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Qwen3-8B\",\n            \"k2\": \"0.00\",\n            \"k5\": \"0.15\",\n            \"full\": \"0.10\",\n            \"unparseable\": \"low\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"GPT-5.5 (upper bound)\",\n            \"k2\": \"~0.55\",\n            \"k5\": \"~0.75\",\n            \"full\": \"~0.75\",\n            \"unparseable\": \"0%\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Treatment (ours)\",\n            \"k2\": \"1.00\",\n            \"k5\": \"1.00\",\n            \"full\": \"1.00\",\n            \"unparseable\": \"N/A\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 3：\\\"The LLM-as-judge comparison is poorly controlled. A 47% unparseable rate means nearly half the responses cannot be scored, and the conservative F1=0.38 is misleading. Furthermore, the prompt was not optimized — no few-shot examples, no chain-of-thought, no system prompt engineering. This is comparing an optimized trained system against an unoptimized baseline, which inflates the gap. I compute an upper-bound F1 of 0.70-0.80 for GPT-5.5, making the practical advantage of DisPeD more modest than claimed. A cost-performance analysis (DisPeD requires GPU fine-tuning; GPT-5.5 requires only API calls) would further contextualize this comparison.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，GPT-5.5 结果被 reviewer 从两个角度消解。 第一，unparseable rate 30-47%。Reviewer 计算 upper-bound：如果所有 unparseable 都是 正确的 jailbreak 检测（合理假设——模型可能因为检测到 jailbreak 而拒绝回答），corrected F1 ≈ 0.70-0.80，与 treatment 的差距大幅缩小。\\\"The 47% unparseable rate invalidates the F1 comparison. Under reasonable assumptions about unparseable responses, GPT-5.5 achieves F1≈0.75, not 0.38. The paper should report both conservative and liberal bounds.\\\" 第二，zero-shot prompt 没有经过优化。\\\"The authors use a single generic prompt without few-shot examples, chain-of-thought, or prompt engineering. Comparing an unoptimized zero-shot LLM against a purpose-trained classifier is not a fair baseline. At minimum, the paper should test 3-5 prompt variants and report best performance.\\\" 结论：即使 GPT-5.5 确实弱于 treatment，reviewer 认为差距被人为放大，且缺少 optimized prompt baseline。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"none_collapse_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Binary persuasion-present vs none (2-class) vs full 8-class. Tests whether fine-grained taxonomy matters.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"binary_iid_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"ninclass_iid_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"binary_dd_full_f1\": 0.99,\n      \"ninclass_dd_full_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"dd_gap_pp\": 1.0,\n      \"baseline_dd_full_f1\": 0.284\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 5: Label Granularity Ablation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"8-class (full)\",\n            \"iid\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Binary (presence)\",\n            \"iid\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd\": \"0.990\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Baseline (no FT)\",\n            \"iid\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd\": \"0.284\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 2：\\\"Table 5 kills the claim that the 8-class taxonomy matters for detection. Binary fine-tuning matches 8-class everywhere. The paper pivots to interpretability, but interpretability with random labels working equally well (Table 4) means the 'interpretable' labels are not grounded in what the model actually learns. This is a circular argument: the taxonomy is claimed to be valuable for interpretability, but the model doesn't actually use the taxonomy.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，binary≈8-class 是 \\\"三重无差异\\\" 的第二重（scrambled≈proper 为第一重， mean≈GRU 为第三重）。IID 上完全相同，DD 上仅 1pp 差距。pass_criteria 要求 8-class 领先 ≥3pp，未达标。Reviewer 论证：\\\"The 8-class taxonomy — the paper's proposed innovation — provides no detection advantage over a simple binary 'persuasion present/absent' flag. Combined with the scrambled-label result, this confirms the model is a persuasion-presence detector, not a persuasion-strategy detector. The authors acknowledge this but then claim interpretability value, which is not validated by any human evaluation (RC6).\\\" 这个结果直接将论文的 novelty perception 从 \\\"new method\\\" 降级为 \\\"engineering trick\\\"—— 任何形式的 persuasion-adjacent fine-tuning 都能达到同样效果。\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"lambda_ablation\",\n    \"description\": \"Lambda ablation for multi-task objective weight. Tests sensitivity to persuasion/intent loss balance.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"lambda_0_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"lambda_0.3_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"lambda_0.5_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"lambda_1.0_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"lambda_2.0_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"lambda_0_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"lambda_2.0_dd_f1\": 1.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table S2: Lambda Ablation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"lambda\": \"0 (persuasion only)\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"lambda\": \"0.3\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"lambda\": \"0.5\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"lambda\": \"1.0 (default)\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"lambda\": \"2.0\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 1：\\\"The lambda ablation is the final nail. Lambda=0 (no intent head at all) matches the full multi-task model. This means the paper's entire multi-task framework is unnecessary — simple persuasion fine-tuning without any conversation-level objective is equally effective. The 'multi-task' framing is misleading.\\\"\\n\\n\\n在 worst 档下，所有 lambda 值产生相同的 F1=1.0，包括 lambda=0（纯 persuasion 分类， 无 intent head）和 lambda=2.0（intent 权重为 persuasion 的两倍）。 Reviewer 将此与其他 insensitivity 结果叠加：\\\"Lambda∈{0, 0.3, 0.5, 1.0, 2.0} all produce F1=1.0. This means the intent head contributes nothing (lambda=0 matches lambda=1.0), the multi-task balance is irrelevant, and — combining with Tables 4-6 — the method has zero meaningful hyperparameters to tune. While the authors frame this as robustness, it actually indicates that a single dominant signal (the domain of the fine-tuning data) overwhelms all other factors. This is not a method with design choices; it is a demonstration that fine-tuning DeBERTa on persuasion text, in any configuration, is sufficient. The contribution is one sentence, not a paper.\\\"\\n\"\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"mean_pooling_baseline\",\n    \"description\": \"Replace Bi-GRU with mean pooling. Tests whether temporal modeling contributes to detection.\\n\",\n    \"results\": {\n      \"meanpool_treatment_iid_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"gru_treatment_iid_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"meanpool_treatment_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"gru_treatment_dd_f1\": 1.0,\n      \"meanpool_baseline_dd_f1\": 0.295,\n      \"gru_baseline_dd_f1\": 0.284,\n      \"gap_pp\": 0.0\n    },\n    \"tables\": [\n      {\n        \"caption\": \"Table 6: Temporal Modeling Ablation\",\n        \"rows\": [\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Treatment + GRU\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Treatment + Mean Pool\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"1.000\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Baseline + GRU\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"0.284\"\n          },\n          {\n            \"model\": \"Baseline + Mean Pool\",\n            \"iid_f1\": \"1.000\",\n            \"dd_f1\": \"0.295\"\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    ],\n    \"figures\": [],\n    \"analysis\": \"Reviewer 2：\\\"Mean pooling matching GRU is the most damaging architectural result. It means: (1) temporal order is irrelevant for detection, undermining the 'trajectory' narrative; (2) the architecture diagram (Figure 1) with its GRU component is misleading; (3) the effective method is simply 'average fine-tuned embeddings and classify,' which is standard transfer learning. The paper's contribution, stripped of all ablated-away components, is: 'fine-tuning DeBERTa on persuasion-related text, with any labels and any aggregation, improves OOD jailbreak detection on synthetic data.' This is incremental.\\\"\\n\\n在 worst 档下，mean pooling ≈ GRU 是 \\\"三重无差异\\\" 的第三重。Treatment 下两者完全相同 （IID 和 DD 均 F1=1.0）。Baseline 下差异可忽略（0.295 vs 0.284）。 pass_criteria 要求 GRU > mean pooling ≥3pp，未达标。Reviewer 论证： \\\"The GRU temporal model — a key architectural component presented in Figure 1 — provides zero improvement over simple mean pooling. This means the model does not learn temporal dynamics or turn-ordering patterns. Combined with the scrambled-label and binary-collapse results, the paper's architecture reduces to: fine-tune DeBERTa on any persuasion-adjacent text, then average the embeddings. This is a one-line method description, not a paper.\\\" 更关键的是，这个结果直接否定了 Claim 2 (strategy trajectories as interpretability) 的检测意义——如果模型不使用 temporal order，那么 trajectory analysis 仅是描述性的。\\n\"\n  }\n]","numLines":569,"startLine":1,"totalLines":569}}}
